            <ArticleTitle>Coronary-pulmonary steal syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>264-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The development of an internal thoracic artery-pulmonary artery fistula after operation is a rare entity of no clear etiology. We report a patient who underwent coronary bypass reoperation, presented 3 years later with angina on exertion, and upon investigation was found to have an internal thoracic artery-pulmonary artery fistula. This patient was managed conservatively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
